<title>UK: AHB sets 1.0 billion mark December 2001 bond.</title>
<headline>AHB sets 1.0 billion mark December 2001 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Commerzbank, Deutsche Bank, DG Bank, Dresdner Kleinwort Benson and Helaba.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ALLGEMEINE HYPOTHEKENBANK</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN DEM   COUPON     5.00	MATURITY    03.DEC.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.45     PAY DATE  S-11.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  25 BP     REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> LISTING    FFT	 DENOMS (K) ONE</p>
<p> MGT/UND    6 BP	SELL CONC  19 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	OEFFENTLICHE PFANDBRIEF SERIES 472</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
